{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Hear us, etc.</b> Meaning: Accept our words that we say to you to do — namely, that you choose the choicest grave among the graves and bury your dead, and you need not ask permission to say, 'Such-and-such a place I desire,' nor to pay its value. And the reason is <b>none of us will withhold his grave from you</b>, etc. — behold, grant of permission is hereby given to you. And their reason is so that his dead not be detained before him, as he stated in his plea. And his saying <b>a prince</b>, etc. will be explained shortly:" "<b>My lord.</b> Meaning 'master,' and it is not an honorific singular form, like <b>Adoni-tzedek</b> in Joshua (Joshua 10:1)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:49.014050606Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}